{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-05-05","source":"Senate","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on the Judiciary.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"10000","actionDate":"2025-05-05","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in Senate","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/1589","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"C001095","fullName":"Sen. Cotton, Tom [R-AR]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AR"},{"bioguideId":"H001089","fullName":"Sen. Hawley, Josh [R-MO]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"B001319","fullName":"Sen. Britt, Katie Boyd [R-AL]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AL"},{"bioguideId":"T000278","fullName":"Sen. Tuberville, Tommy [R-AL]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AL"},{"bioguideId":"B001305","fullName":"Sen. Budd, Ted [R-NC]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"L000577","fullName":"Sen. Lee, Mike [R-UT]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"UT"},{"bioguideId":"E000295","fullName":"Sen. Ernst, Joni [R-IA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"C001075","fullName":"Sen. Cassidy, Bill [R-LA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"LA"},{"bioguideId":"L000575","fullName":"Sen. Lankford, James [R-OK]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OK"},{"bioguideId":"M001242","fullName":"Sen. Moreno, Bernie [R-OH]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"S001232","fullName":"Sen. Sheehy, Tim [R-MT]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-05","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MT"},{"bioguideId":"H001079","fullName":"Sen. Hyde-Smith, Cindy [R-MS]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-31","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T06:27:46+00:00","id":"s1589-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-05","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-05","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"1589","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Immigration","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"G000386","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Grassley, Chuck [R-IA]","party":"R","state":"IA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-05-05","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Immigration Parole Reform Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill limits the authority of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to grant immigration parole (i.e., give official permission for an individual to enter and temporarily remain in the United States).</p><p>Specifically, the bill (1) limits what qualifies as an urgent humanitarian reason or a significant public benefit that would justify granting parole, and (2) prohibits granting parole based on an individual's membership in a defined class of individuals.</p><p>An urgent humanitarian reason is limited to medical emergencies, the death of a close family member, and to green card applicants returning to the United States after temporary travel abroad. A significant public benefit is limited to assisting the U.S. government in a law enforcement matter.</p><p>Individuals granted parole on the basis of an urgent humanitarian reason or a significant public benefit are not permitted to work while in the United States.</p><p>Additionally, the bill provides statutory authority for DHS to grant parole to certain Cuban nationals and to certain family members of active-duty Armed Forces members.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2026-04-14T22:38:43Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Immigration Parole Reform Act of 2025","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-08-10T11:51:27Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-08-10T11:51:27Z"}
